# Trading dashboard UX (PythonTrading)

Stack: **Python 3.11+**, **CustomTkinter** (`dashboard_app.py`), Streamlit backup (`dashboard.py`, `portal.py`). Dark mode default.

## 1. Cognitive load (progressive disclosure)

- **Primary surface:** equity, cash, position status, bot state, active book (Alpaca Live/Paper) — always visible in header + metric row.
- **Secondary:** regime, wisdom, sleeve exposure → **Overview** tab only.
- **Tertiary:** trade log, charts, API keys, account switcher → **tabs** or **☰ hamburger menu**; never clutter the default view.
- **During bot execution:** emphasize **Bot: Running/Stopped** and **LIVE vs Paper** banner; hide charts unless user opens Charts tab.
- Do not add new always-visible widgets without removing or collapsing something else.

## 2. Visual hierarchy (F-pattern)

Top bar left → right (high attention):

1. ☰ accounts menu
2. App name
3. **Active book** badge (Alpaca Live / Paper)
4. Username (muted)

Below header:

1. **Metric cards** (Equity, Cash %, Invested %, P&L, Market) — top-left, largest numbers
2. **Primary CTAs** (Start Bot / Stop Bot / Refresh) — footer or header right; **Stop Bot** uses confirmation; live actions use extra friction (confirm + warning copy)

Fitts's Law: primary actions ≥ 88px wide, reachable without crossing the full window.

## 3. Error mitigation & color

Palette (`dashboard_app.py` `COLORS`):

- Background `#141414`, cards `#1e1e1e`, muted text `#9ca3af`
- **Green** `#22c55e` — positive P&L, bot running (not generic UI)
- **Amber** `#f59e0b` — stopped/warning, small-account mode (not panic)
- **Red** `#dc2626` / `#7f1d1d` — **live money banner, destructive actions, errors only** — never for labels, borders, or decoration (avoid alert fatigue)
- Live vs paper must be instantly distinguishable (banner + title book badge)

High-risk actions require:

- `messagebox.askyesno` with explicit consequence text
- Live key save → confirm dialog (already implemented)
- Stop bot → confirm (already implemented)

Color-blind: do not rely on red vs green alone — pair with text ("Running", "LIVE TRADING", "+$").

## 4. Trading mental models

- **Positions:** table columns — Ticker, Qty, Entry, Current, P&L $, P&L % (industry standard)
- **Trades:** closed round-trips — Ticker, Qty, Entry, Exit, P&L $, P&L %, Bought, Sold (newest first)
- **Order book:** N/A (bot-driven); show **sleeve caps / exposure** instead of fake order UI
- Button states: every `CTkButton` needs distinct `fg_color` / `hover_color`; disabled = `state="disabled"` + muted color
- Dark theme only for desktop monitor; no white flashes on refresh

## 5. Multi-account (books)

- One portal login; **☰ menu** switches books (`modules/trading_books.py`)
- Keys and bot state isolated per book under `data/portal/users/<user>/books/<book_id>/`
- UI must show **which book** is active before Start Bot

## When adding features

Before merging UI changes, verify:

- [ ] Default view still shows equity + bot state in &lt; 3 seconds of scanning
- [ ] New config lives in tab, menu, or dialog — not the main canvas
- [ ] Live/destructive actions have confirmation
- [ ] Red used only for urgent/risk states
